SetupBodyRuleSatisfiedTest
├── when the body has no clauses
│   └── it should return false naming clause zero
├── when every clause has a threshold of zero
│   ├── when no place is filled
│   │   └── it should return false naming clause zero
│   └── when places are filled
│       └── it should return false naming clause zero
├── when a zero clause sits beside a positive clause
│   ├── when the positive clause meets its threshold
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── when the positive clause misses its threshold
│   │   └── it should return false naming the positive clause
│   └── when only the zero clause's places are filled
│       └── it should return false naming the positive clause
├── when the filled count equals the threshold
│   └── it should return true
├── when the filled count is one below the threshold
│   └── it should return false naming that clause
├── when the filled count exceeds the threshold
│   └── it should return true
├── when a clause's threshold exceeds its credential count
│   └── it should return false naming that clause even with every place filled
├── when the rule is met and places past the end are filled
│   └── it should return true ignoring the places past the end
├── when a single clause at the widest threshold lists one credential more
│   ├── when as many places as the widest threshold are filled
│   │   └── it should return true
│   └── when one place fewer than the widest threshold is filled
│       └── it should return false naming that clause
├── when several clauses miss their thresholds
│   └── it should name the first failing clause in body order
├── when an earlier clause is met and a later clause misses
│   └── it should name the later clause
├── when every clause meets its threshold
│   └── it should return true
├── when one credential repeats at two places
│   └── it should count both places
├── when the filled places sit in another clause
│   └── it should not count them toward this clause
├── when a place repeats the previous place
│   └── it should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing naming the repeated place
├── when a place repeats in a set that misses its threshold
│   └── it should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing rather than report the missed clause
├── when a place is below the previous place
│   └── it should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing naming the lower place
└── when each place is exactly one above the previous place
    └── it should count every place
